From: Uke platform maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: mark Cliffs GPIO as a GPIO function

The generic pinmux GPIO predicate now reads PINFUNCTION_FLAG_GPIO.
Use the standard Qualcomm GPIO initializer so a GPIO pinctrl state and
the owning GPIO consumer can coexist under strict mux ownership.
This fixes the observed Uke WCD939x GPIO 119 double-claim failure.

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-cliffs.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-cliffs.c
@@ -1563,7 +1563,7 @@
 };
 
 static const struct pinfunction cliffs_functions[] = {
-	FUNCTION(gpio),
+	MSM_GPIO_PIN_FUNCTION(gpio),
 	FUNCTION(HOST2WLAN_SOL),
 	FUNCTION(RESOUT_GPIO_N),
 	FUNCTION(aoss_cti),
